ing to be any content  this week because they didn't want to  save or steal but next week they're  going to be adding three new outfits per  hero new effects and they were called  the optical illusion spotter and Virgo  for the outfits along with the bat out  effect for executions in emotes which I  will show to you right now  you  you  you  so that was pretty cool though I kind of  I think my personal favorite was the  splatter effect can't wait to put that  on some of my characters when they come  out though  but anyway next up is they showed off  some of the new epic tier armor for some  of the characters which is on screen now  I really do enjoy some of these items  especially warden's in my opinion they  did I did they did show Raiders and  Kent's A's but I liked worden  specifically because it just kind of was  a lot more shinier and stuff like that  but they were only the weapons they  didn't really show off much of the gear  it was just the weapon items and such  next up is matchmaking now takes into  account your reputation level making it  easier to find players of your skill  level which you will have and you will  probably have to select your hero before  matchmaking and the beginning that if  you are a player that plays a lot but is  really garbage then you'll be matched up  players that play a lot but are really  garbage so trying to make it exactly how  you play so if you are really good but  haven't really played too much then  you'll get matched up of players such as  those if you have so if you have a lot  of reputation you're going to be matched  up with characters that also have a lot  of reputation on them is like little  magical numbers you're like total rep  there now in terms of the hero buffs  Raider finally got the buff that we've  been looking for and now changes it so  that every heavy or zone attack can now  be canceled into the stunning tap move  which is the move where he jumps forward  and then slams the butt of his little  axe into y